%N A399582 Numbers k not divisible by 3 such that at least one of 3+2k and 3+4k is composite.
%C A399582 Numbers k not divisible by 3 that are missing from the sequence of k for which 3+2k and 3+4k are both prime.
%F A399582 a(n) = A360735(n) / 2.
%e A399582 For a(1) = 8, 8 is not divisible by 3 and 3+2.8 = 19 is prime, but 3+4.8 = 35 is composite so 8 is a term.
